# ── AT command templates ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Format is line-based and human-readable:
#   ## Group            a section header shown in the drop-down list
#   # What it does       a description of the command right below it
#   AT+CSQ               the command itself — sent to the modem verbatim
#                        (several commands joined by ';' run in one session)
# A blank line ends an entry. Lines starting with '#' are NEVER sent to the
# modem — they are comments/descriptions only. Descriptions are translated in
# the web UI; your own text is shown as written. Edit this file freely — it
# is a user file and survives package upgrades.

## Identity

# Modem information
ATI

# Manufacturer, model, firmware
AT+CGMI;+CGMM;+CGMR

# IMEI
AT+CGSN

## Signal and network

# Signal quality
AT+CSQ

# Extended signal quality
AT+CESQ

# Operator
AT+COPS?

# LTE registration
AT+CEREG?

# 5G registration
AT+C5GREG?

## Data session

# PDP contexts (APN)
AT+CGDCONT?

# PDP addresses
AT+CGPADDR

# Packet-service attach
AT+CGATT?

## SIM

# SIM PIN status
AT+CPIN?

# IMSI
AT+CIMI

# Own number
AT+CPBS="ON";+CNUM

## Radio control

# Modem clock
AT+CCLK?

# Radio function mode
AT+CFUN?

# Reboot the modem
AT+CFUN=1,1

# Radio off
AT+CFUN=4

# Radio on
AT+CFUN=1

## Phonebook — edit the number before sending

# Write a number to the SIM
AT+CSCS="IRA";+CPBS="ON";+CPBW=1,"+79876543210",145,"Number"
